> See also https://www.w3.org/Bugs/Public/show_bug.cgi?id=21674.

That's a somewhat different situation: that's for cases when you try to get crossOriginWindowProxy.foo where "foo" is a subframe name of that cross-origin window.  This issue is about sameOriginWindowProxy.foo where "foo" is the name of a subframe that's cross-origin, and in particular where "foo" comes from setting `window.name` in the cross-origin page.

@zetafunction, thank you for bringing this up. I'd like to better understand IE's behavior here.  Do they make the `.name` setter a no-op in subframes?  In cross-origin subframes?  In general?  Do you have testcases offhand for the various cases here, or do we need to put some together?

@bzbarsky, I've attached the test cases I was trying.

For IE, it looks like the .name setter is a no-op in all subframes. It still works on top-level frames though.

The test cases I've been trying are at https://ithildin.com/tests/window/name.html.
